# Engineering

Details: [`docs/conventions.md`](../../docs/conventions.md). Human process: `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Layout

- Solution file: **`Txfio.slnx` only** (do not create or keep `.sln`)
- Implementation under `src/Txfio/`
- Tests under `tests/Txfio.Tests/` mirroring src folders (`Foo.cs` → `FooTests.cs`)
- Lasting decisions: `docs/design.md`, `docs/roadmap.md`, `docs/conventions.md`
- Do not put lasting decisions only in `.dev/`

## Targets

- TFM: `net8.0` (not `net8.0-windows`)
- Runtime guarantee: Windows (NTFS/SMB)
- Test framework: xUnit
- Public surface: contracts only; implementations `internal`; `InternalsVisibleTo` for tests

## Analyzers and format

- Nullable enabled; treat warnings as errors
- StyleCop.Analyzers + built-in code analysis via shared `Directory.Build.props`
- Format with `dotnet format` / `.editorconfig` (LF)
- Private fields: `_camelCase` (including static). Constants: PascalCase. Do not prefix members with `this.` unless required for disambiguation
- StyleCop SA1101 / SA1306 / SA1309 / SA1310 / SA1311 are disabled so .NET field naming wins
- Strict XML docs on public API **and** `public` members of internal types, plus internal types/members (`documentInternalElements`). Do not block tests/private on doc requirements
- Interface names must be prefixed with `I`. SA1302 stays enabled
- Comments (XML docs / inline) in **Japanese**; do not end them with `。` or `.` (SA1629 disabled)
- New or changed Japanese XML docs in `src/` must be reviewed by Gemini for natural wording before the PR is ready (`.cursor/rules/japanese-docs.mdc`)
- Test method names: natural Japanese, plus 前提 / 手順 / 期待 in remarks
- Library `await` uses `ConfigureAwait(false)`. Do not Dispose caller-owned `Stream`s
- Paths: normalized absolute, compare `OrdinalIgnoreCase`
- No logging framework in the library
- No `using X = System.IO.File` aliases; fully qualify when names collide

## Verification gate

- Windows: `./build.ps1` before merge (restore → format verify → build → test) on **`Txfio.slnx`**
- Linux: do **not** run `./build.ps1`. Run restore / format verify / build / `dotnet test`. Before a PR, all tests must pass except those skipped as `Windows 専用` (`WindowsFact`). This does not replace the Windows merge gate
- Tests that depend on Windows-only behavior (junctions, drive letters, open files that cannot be renamed or deleted) use `[WindowsFact("reason")]`
- GitHub Actions workflow may exist but **must not be assumed runnable** while Actions are restricted
- Crash injection / SMB tests are required only when the Issue acceptance says so
